    {
      "content": "Amanda\u2019s Monday briefing: Catch up in minutes with these 7 stories",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "type": "title",
      "subtype": "h1",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "content": "Inflation. Internet bills. Child tax credits. Britney Spears. Texas Democrats. Voting rights. South Africa.",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "type": "deck"
    },
    {
      "adsUrl": "https://d2i9ke5o9i0vh8.cloudfront.net/washpost-audio-articles/IDZZQLKQEJBLHCI57ZWEKJV63U/20211007-151966.666/current.mp3?awCollectionId=/topics/the-seven&awEpisodeId=IDZZQLKQEJBLHCI57ZWEKJV63U",
      "rawUrl": "https://audio-articles.sandbox.lionfish.media.aws.wapo.pub/IDZZQLKQEJBLHCI57ZWEKJV63U/20211007-151966.666/current.mp3",
      "type": "audio",
      "subtype": "audio-article"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "imageURL": "https://arc-anglerfish-washpost-sandbox-sandbox-washpost.s3.amazonaws.com/public/5NQHD4ACP4I6ZB7APYD33HHCOA.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 3388,
      "imageHeight": 2259,
      "image_type": "photograph",
      "widthFactor": "full-bleed",
      "fullcaption": "Dog trainer Ali Smith practices a jumping trick with her dog, Indie, a German Shepherd mix, at Baker Park in downtown Frederick, Md., July 30, 2021. As a full-time dog trainer, Smith works with many clients in Frederick County and trains a variety of dogs with different ages and breeds. (Katina Zentz/The Frederick News-Post via AP)",
      "blurb": "Dog trainer Ali Smith practices a jumping trick with her dog, Indie, a German Shepherd mix, at Baker Park in downtown Frederick, Md., July 30, 2021. As a full-time dog trainer, Smith works with many clients in Frederick County and trains a variety of dogs with different ages and breeds. (Katina Zentz/The Frederick News-Post via AP)"
    },
    {
      "content": "By Amanda \"The Bozz\" Bozzi",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "type": "byline",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Amanda \"The Bozz\" Bozzi"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "content": 1631286468555,
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "type": "date"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "1",
      "subhead_level": 2,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>Yes, your groceries (and most everything else)</b> are more expensive than ever. \ud83d\ude15",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>Bad news first: Inflation is rising. </b>Prices <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2021/07/13/inflation-cpi-june-prices-fed/?itid=lk_inline_manual_4\">jumped 5.4 percent</a> in June compared to last year. That\u2019s the largest spike since 2008.",
        "<b>How big of a deal is this? </b>Experts are divided over whether the increases are here to stay or are a temporary part of recovery from the pandemic."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "2",
      "subhead_level": 3,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>Millions of parents will get $300 from the IRS</b> deposited in their bank accounts starting tomorrow.",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>What are these payments? </b>The <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2021/07/13/child-tax-credit-payments-irs/?itid=lk_inline_manual_8\">child tax credit</a> was expanded under the latest coronavirus relief bill and will be distributed monthly for the rest of 2021.",
        "<b>Who qualifies?</b> Parents of children 5 and under can receive up to $300 a month. Parents of children ages 6-17 can get up to $250 a month.",
        "<b>How do I sign up?</b> It should be automatic. The IRS is pulling information from tax returns, like it did for the stimulus checks."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "3",
      "subhead_level": 3,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>President Biden called GOP-led voting restrictions</b> the biggest threat to democracy since the Civil War.",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>His speech yesterday </b>was an attempt to give new momentum to passing a <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/biden-voting-speech/2021/07/13/afd91f7a-e3d9-11eb-8aa5-5662858b696e_story.html?itid=lk_inline_manual_14\">law that protects voting rights</a>.",
        "<b>What Biden did not do: </b>Call for the Senate to change the filibuster, which advocates say is the only way to get a bill on voting rights passed."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "4",
      "subhead_level": 3,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>Dozens of Democratic lawmakers from Texas who left the state</b> to block restrictive voting legislation are in D.C. pleading with Congress to act.",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>This is the second time this year</b> they have <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/biden-voting-speech/2021/07/13/afd91f7a-e3d9-11eb-8aa5-5662858b696e_story.html?itid=lk_inline_manual_19\">staged a walkout</a> to avoid a vote on this issue.",
        "<b>GOP lawmakers in the Texas House </b>directed state troopers to arrest the missing lawmakers when they return to Texas, a move backed by the governor."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "5",
      "subhead_level": 3,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>Britney\u2019s back in court today</b> in the high-profile fight over her conservatorship.",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/arts-entertainment/2021/07/14/britney-spears-conservatorship-court-case/?itid=lk_inline_manual_23\"><b>What\u2019s happening?</b></a><b> </b>Spears herself is not expected to speak, but there could be updates as to what happens next in her battle for independence.",
        "<b>What is a conservatorship again?</b> It\u2019s a legal arrangement that places a vulnerable adult under the supervision of another adult. In this case, her father."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "6",
      "subhead_level": 3,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>South Africa is in the grips of the most violent protests</b> since the end of apartheid rule, with 72 people dead so far.",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>The </b><a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2021/07/13/south-africa-zuma-protests-violence/?itid=lk_inline_manual_27\"><b>protests began</b></a><b> when </b>Jacob Zuma, the country\u2019s first Zulu president, was arrested July 7.",
        "<b>Lootings have gutted businesses</b> and blockaded major supply routes, leading to fuel and food shortages."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "subhead",
      "mime": "text/plain",
      "content": "7",
      "subhead_level": 3,
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<b>Internet providers jack up your bill</b> using their lock on neighborhoods \u2014 and a lack of rules.",
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "subtype": "unordered",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": [
        "<b>Part of the problem is a lack of competition: </b>About <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2021/07/13/internet-cable-bills/?itid=lk_inline_manual_32\">200 million people</a> live in places with only one or two options for reliable, fast Internet.",
        "<b>Biden has asked the FCC</b> to address pricing issues by requiring a \u201cnutrition label\u201d for broadband service, like you get with packaged food."
      ],
      "style": "briefs"
    },
    {
      "type": "sanitized_html",
      "subtype": "paragraph",
      "mime": "text/html",
      "content": "<i>Want to catch up quickly with \u201cThe 7\u201d every morning? </i><a href=\"https://wapo.onelink.me/e76N/782c66a8\"><i>Download The Post\u2019s app</i></a><i> and turn on alert notifications for The 7.</i>",
      "style": "briefs"
    }
  ],
